However, the time intervals between the milestones generally are the same as those the Bureau 
establishes for its other auctions.  The revised target dates are based on the 
revised auction start date and the revised auction closing date.  For licenses in the 30 MHz spectrum 
block, the revised licensing target dates are based on a presumption of an auction duration of six weeks 
from the March 6, 2001 starting date of Auction No. 31.  In addition, the revised licensing target dates 
take into account the additional time needed to process applications in which the applicant seeks a tribal 
land bidding credit.   


